From 22f4781fc60b68eaf9d083841258320271f2cc27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:29:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] serve: background reads (STRATA_SERVER_READS=1, from
 ll7-reads2 99602e75 + c87b2d7b + d9e25df3, opt-in)

The server half of stage-2 parallel reads, ported as one diff (bda03b22..ll7-reads2 HEAD, serve/ only) onto the
srv-1106 line: an admission with at least STRATA_READS_BG_MIN (8192) new tokens names a free top-row park slot (bg=)
to an engine run with STRATA_READS=N (INFO reads=N reads_row=k); BREAD hands the lines and the admission slot back,
BPP/BREADY/BRDONE come on the park slot's queue, and the finish takes the control lines first (prio) and is sent again
with yslot=<park>. STRATA_READS_SOLO=1 (default 0) lets a long lone request go the same way. Unset (or an engine
without INFO reads): no bg= is ever sent and every path is as before (test_unset_never_sends_bg).

Composition with this line: _take_control keeps 90f73293's signature (total, since: STRATA_ADMIT_BY_NEW) and gains
prio; the prio entry is [len, arrival, False, len(, ids)], so _admit_next (ordered entries only) never ranks it and
_entry_new finds its ids at e[4]. The background decision counts only what slots hold (_new_tokens), not the admit
estimate (the 90f73293 rule). admitted() is idempotent, so the re-sent BGEN after BREADY notes nothing twice. A
stream write timeout (c08fd2ec port) during a background read closes the generator: the bg_wait branch BSTOPs the read
and frees the park on the engine's BRDONE/BREADY. Conflict resolved: the _take_control signature and docstring only.

Tests: serve/test_reads.py (10, fake engine) and the full serve suite (918, 11 skipped) pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
